# Visual workbench environment.
# Copy to `.env.visual` (or export in your shell) and adjust as needed.
# No secrets belong in this file — it only carries public URLs.

# Live reference site used for measured comparison.
REFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://www.merterelektronik.com

# Local application under development.
#
# WARNING — port 3000 is the Next.js default for every project on this machine.
# During setup, localhost:3000 was already answering with an unrelated project
# ("VoltEdge"). A stray dev server will be captured happily and you will spend
# an hour diffing the wrong application.
#
# `capture-local.mjs` prints the served <title> before it captures — read that
# line. If it is not this project, stop the other server or set a distinct port
# here and in the storefront's dev script.
LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: set to 1 in CI so Playwright never tries to boot a dev server
# and so the reference-capture project is skipped on network-restricted runners.
# CI=1
